WEBVTT

00:00.330 --> 00:03.889
A contractor says a replacement part was ordered on Monday.

00:04.285 --> 00:07.640
When you ask for an update, they hesitate and look away.

00:08.048 --> 00:09.336
You suspect a lie.

00:09.744 --> 00:13.635
The delay matters, but the gesture does not tell you why it happened.

00:14.030 --> 00:18.902
Start with what you need to establish: whether the part was ordered, when, and when it

00:18.915 --> 00:20.267
is expected to arrive.

00:21.288 --> 00:26.505
Bond and DePaulo combined findings from research reports about truth-or-lie judgments.

00:26.914 --> 00:31.455
Without the independent records an investigation might provide, participants were

00:31.468 --> 00:34.593
right about fifty-four times out of a hundred on average.

00:35.001 --> 00:39.516
They classified truths correctly about sixty-one times out of a hundred, and

00:39.529 --> 00:41.022
lies about forty-seven.

00:41.430 --> 00:45.167
Those figures are research averages, not the probability that

00:45.180 --> 00:46.595
this contractor is lying.

00:47.622 --> 00:52.711
Vrij, Hartwig and Granhag reviewed research on body language and deception.

00:53.107 --> 00:56.564
Known bodily signs of lying were weak and unreliable.

00:56.947 --> 01:00.110
Avoiding eye contact does not establish dishonesty.

01:00.479 --> 01:05.237
Combining several uncertain gestures does not create a reliable lie test.

01:05.646 --> 01:09.510
You can notice discomfort and offer time to check the details without

01:09.523 --> 01:10.939
deciding what caused it.

01:11.955 --> 01:16.623
Corroboration is additional evidence that supports a claim, especially from

01:16.636 --> 01:17.950
an independent source.

01:18.334 --> 01:22.773
A supplier’s dated order confirmation could support the contractor’s account.

01:23.142 --> 01:25.413
Check what the record actually shows.

01:25.822 --> 01:30.464
A quotation can show an enquiry without showing that an order was completed.

01:30.860 --> 01:35.133
Records can be incomplete or wrong too; their source and scope matter.

01:36.163 --> 01:41.610
The High-Value Detainee Interrogation Group, managed by the FBI, reviewed research

01:41.623 --> 01:42.847
on questioning people.

01:43.256 --> 01:48.396
Its report supports gathering information and building cooperation without coercion.

01:48.805 --> 01:53.486
It does not validate everything sold as an FBI technique, or establish that an

01:53.499 --> 01:58.116
investigative method transfers unchanged to a child, friend or customer.

01:58.524 --> 02:03.192
A former investigator’s story is different from a study comparing outcomes.

02:04.205 --> 02:06.782
Ask what a method’s result actually was.

02:07.191 --> 02:11.655
Did people speak more, provide more facts, provide more accurate facts,

02:11.885 --> 02:13.135
or confess more often?

02:13.543 --> 02:15.188
Those are different outcomes.

02:15.584 --> 02:20.762
For this repair, ordinary questions may be enough: What confirmation did you receive?

02:21.131 --> 02:22.394
Could you forward it?

02:22.803 --> 02:27.050
What can we agree if there is still no confirmed delivery date by Friday?

02:28.080 --> 02:32.799
If visitors are arriving soon, you may want to accept vague reassurance because you

02:32.812 --> 02:34.139
need the repair finished.

02:34.548 --> 02:38.719
If another contractor let you down, you may suspect this one too quickly.

02:39.114 --> 02:42.507
Neither feeling establishes whether this order was placed.

02:42.890 --> 02:47.073
Ask whether you would want the same evidence if the answer were one you disliked.

02:48.122 --> 02:50.532
If the dates do not match, ask why.

02:50.916 --> 02:54.985
A misunderstanding, an error or a lie could explain the difference.

02:55.368 --> 02:57.638
A smooth answer is not proof either.

02:58.046 --> 03:02.995
You may still be able to request a reliable delivery plan or choose another supplier.

03:03.391 --> 03:07.970
Repeated missed commitments can justify changing an arrangement without proving

03:07.982 --> 03:09.424
every motive behind them.

03:10.455 --> 03:14.906
When an answer matters to a decision, ask: What would help me check that?

03:15.316 --> 03:20.443
Identify the claim, seek relevant information, and note what remains unknown.

03:20.839 --> 03:24.984
Avoid private surveillance or unnecessary personal information.

03:25.392 --> 03:30.430
The aim is a decision you can explain using evidence, not winning a contest over who

03:30.443 --> 03:31.846
can read someone’s face.
